    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do I pay anything up front? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. There's no design deposit, because a large payment before any code is written doesn't work for most of the business owners I serve. Your first $175 payment starts the build, and the price never changes after that.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why the 12-month minimum? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I build a full custom site for you with nothing collected up front, and the 12-month term is how the math works out on my side. After the first year, the plan runs month to month, and you can cancel with 30 days' written notice.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I cancel early? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The remaining months are due under the agreement, and the agreement governs. Still, nobody likes an early cancellation, and in practice I usually find a reasonable way forward.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What counts as extra work, and what does it cost? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The plan covers your first 10 content pages, the design and build, hosting, security and maintenance, the groundwork for local search, the blog, and unlimited content updates after launch. An extra page beyond the ten included costs $100 per page. Other work outside the plan costs $100 an hour, such as a custom calculator, a connection to an outside booking system, an email-marketing template, or a move from an old platform. I always send a written estimate before that work starts.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Who owns the domain and the site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Your domain is registered in your name, and you control it; I point it at the hosting. On the monthly plan, I own the code. If you cancel, I help you move the domain to a registrar of your choice, and the website goes offline at the end of the term. There's no export of the site and no code buyout.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
